---
metadata: {
    partial_name: "Sign In | Allowed User",
}
---
{%- comment -%}
  The account an emailed sign-in link or code may sign in to. Called with:
    function account = 'account/sign_in/allowed_user', email: email
  Returns { "id": ..., "otp_configured": true|false }. id is blank when no account may sign in.
  Only a user with a client profile may sign in this way: that is a registered Seedling
  account. Other user records (for example contacts created by the CRM) have no client
  profile and are refused, so a link or code never signs in someone who never registered.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign account = {}
  assign account['id'] = ''
  assign account['otp_configured'] = false

  assign email = email | default: '' | append: '' | strip | downcase
  if email == blank
    return account
  endif

  graphql found = 'account/sign_in/find_user', email: email
  assign profile = found.user.client | first
  if found.user.id != blank and profile.id != blank
    assign account['id'] = found.user.id
    if profile.otp_configured == true
      assign account['otp_configured'] = true
    endif
  endif
  return account
-%}
